            "notes": "Which power I take in Round 3 depends on how the first two rounds went.\n- If the long-range style was mostly working (ie, I wasn't dying often), I'll take [Pinpoint Prescription](item_5cfa07d8-7b5d-42df-a9a8-c6a580acb8bc) and start trying to get headshots in-between healing\n- If I was getting dived repeatedly or dying to the enemy's long range attacks, I'll take  [Sleep Regimen](item_28934e4f-0668-482e-b10d-a5d557cc3b1e) to help with survivability\n\n [Pinpoint Prescription](item_5cfa07d8-7b5d-42df-a9a8-c6a580acb8bc) NOTES:\n- While I find they mostly work well together, there's a nonbo/anti-combo between  [Tactical Rifle](item_683d8145-a13e-4ea8-997b-0ed2151b1cac) and [Pinpoint Prescription](item_5cfa07d8-7b5d-42df-a9a8-c6a580acb8bc)\n- With both of them, you cannot hit scoped crit heals, even when aiming for your teammates' heads - I find it's worth the tradeoff because you just so much more reliably can heal your teammates from range\n- You can still hit no-scope heal shots though, so if you're in a situation where you're hip firing, still aim for your allies (and enemy's) heads; I use the \u2665 crosshair and try to point the bottom tip of the heart pointing at the top of their head, as with the large bullet size, you have a decent amount of leeway\n- With  [Pinpoint Prescription](item_5cfa07d8-7b5d-42df-a9a8-c6a580acb8bc) and your increasing amount of weapon damage, your crit shots start hitting very hard, which can make Ana extremely effective at getting eliminations, even with relatively low damage done (\"we have Widowmaker at home\")\n- You have a good chance of getting eliminations even completely by accident while healing the chaotic stadium fights, as a stray bullet will take out a lot of the enemy's health\n\n [Sleep Regimen](item_28934e4f-0668-482e-b10d-a5d557cc3b1e):\n- Most Ana builds seem to take this in the first or third round for good reason - it's great for survivability\n- Here, we're trying to avoid getting hit in the first place simply by being far away from the action - ideally, you don't need the extra health\n- However, if you are getting targeted heavily and dying in the first few rounds, take  [Sleep Regimen](item_28934e4f-0668-482e-b10d-a5d557cc3b1e), and probably [Dash Boots](item_1ec670c7-a465-4ca0-9d16-aeeedab7894e) and  [Tranquilizer](item_2bea20a0-21c0-4a52-b81e-596c17d184b4) as well\n-  [Sleep Regimen](item_28934e4f-0668-482e-b10d-a5d557cc3b1e) give you 50 health + 10 more health for every Sleep Dart you have landed. Notably this includes sleep darts you *already* landed\n- As you've likely landed at least a couple sleep darts in the first few rounds, this should give you at least 80+ health even before you get [Tranquilizer](item_2bea20a0-21c0-4a52-b81e-596c17d184b4) and start spamming sleep darts more often\n- The  [Tranquilizer](item_2bea20a0-21c0-4a52-b81e-596c17d184b4) darts are huge; you only need to aim at the general vicinity of an enemy to sleep them\n- You can often hit sleep darts from long range with  [Tranquilizer](item_2bea20a0-21c0-4a52-b81e-596c17d184b4), just because the darts are so huge; sleeping someone for 6 seconds during a team fight can make a huge difference that isn't recorded in the scoreboard stats",
