            "notes": "ROUND 5:\n- At this point, you pick up whichever of  [Sleep Regimen](item_28934e4f-0668-482e-b10d-a5d557cc3b1e) or  [Pinpoint Prescription](item_5cfa07d8-7b5d-42df-a9a8-c6a580acb8bc) you didn't choose in Round 3\n- Even without [Tranquilizer](item_2bea20a0-21c0-4a52-b81e-596c17d184b4) or a focus on sleep darts,  [Sleep Regimen](item_28934e4f-0668-482e-b10d-a5d557cc3b1e) is likely giving you 100+ HP by round five, helping out with the increased damage this round\n- Still focus on building Weapon Power with items, only get  [Tranquilizer](item_2bea20a0-21c0-4a52-b81e-596c17d184b4) if you feel you need to hit more sleep darts, or need to shoot something like a Mercy or a Juno out of the air - otherwise, just try to get your WP as high as you can\n- As people mostly go for glass canon builds, your sniper rounds scale faster than than most people's HP does, and comparatively, you start hitting really hard\n- I'm not sure if, mathematically you can actually 1-shot people with headshots at this point, but between other sources of damage, a single headshot (and even body shots, if they are already damaged) is usually enough to take out most players\n- Still focus on maintaining as long a range as you can while still keeping LOS, and healing and damaging\n- Because Ana's offensive capabilities start scaling so strongly, you probably want to shift over to focusing more on damage and securing eliminations than healing, but it depends on the game and how much your co-support is focusing on healing",
